From aa8d6d79a50f979460a317c88dac4ed41916f611 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:14:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/46] glm5-next: graph-level dispatch cuts for decode and MTP
 verify

- KDA conv: SILU directly on the SSM_CONV output (no reshape in between), so the
  Vulkan SSM_CONV_SILU fusion fires (-102 dispatches per graph).
- KDA conv, small ubatches (<= 8 tokens per seq): Q/K/V share one conv window
  tensor (one concat of the three conv states), so each rollback group is one
  CPY for Q, K and V together instead of three, and the n>1 transposes need no
  CONT (n=3 verify: 21 -> 9 dispatches per KDA layer).
- Rollback groups: write only s < min(K, n_seq_tokens) conv groups. The GDN op
  writes only min(n_seq_tokens, K) SSM snapshots, so a rollback into an older
  group already restores a stale SSM state; nothing that worked before changes.
- KDA: no CONT of the (contiguous) GDN score view, reshape instead of cont_2d
  for the gated output.
- MoE: build the shared expert before the routed experts (trunk and MTP), so
  its add joins the expert MULTI_ADD (-42).
- DSA indexer: reorder the top-k indices with an I32 get_rows (no f32 casts and
  CONT); the -inf mask is one in-place FILL; zeros, live = exp(sel_mask) and the
  dead-slot dump rows are built once per graph and shared by all indexer layers;
  idx = idx*live + dead_dump (exact, live is 0/1).
- build_attn_mha (MLA): skip the CONT when the permuted output is already
  contiguous (single token).
- Vulkan graph_optimize: do not hoist a UNARY away from a MUL it can fuse with
  while the MUL's other operand is not ready (KDA output gate
  rms_norm(o)*w*sigmoid(g2) now fuses as SIGMOID_MUL).
- test-backend-ops: GLM5_CONV_QKV (concat of transposed views + SSM_CONV_SILU
  on channel views).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
